  "chapter": {
    "number": 42,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(43) A Psalm of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Judge me, O God, and plead my cause, against an ungodly nation: deliver me from the unjust and crafty man.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you, O God, are my strength: therefore have you cast me off? and why do I go sad of countenance, while the enemy oppresses me?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Send forth your light and your truth: they have led me, and brought me to your holy mountain, and to your tabernacles.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And I will go in to the altar of God, to God who gladdens my youth: I will give thanks to you on the harp, O God, my God.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Therefore are you very sad, O my soul? and therefore do you trouble me? Hope in God; for I will give thanks to him, who is the health of my countenance, and my God.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": []
  },
